values ('e1f2a3b4-5c6d-4e21-8a01-1b2c3d4e5f21', 'acting-i', 'Acting I', 'Acting I is a first-year studio course introducing the craft, discipline, vocabulary, and collaborative habits of actor training. Students learn to use body, voice, imagination, attention, and text analysis to create truthful, repeatable behavior under imaginary circumstances. The course balances Stanislavski-based action work, observation, improvisation, ensemble practice, beginner voice/body integration, ethical rehearsal norms, and introductory scene study. The course is designed as the gateway to Acting II, Voice and Movement, production practicum, script analysis, and later advanced performance work. It treats acting as both artistic exploration and professional practice: students take risks, but they do so inside clear structures of consent, preparation, feedback, and care.');

